---
import DiagramShell from "./DiagramShell.astro";
import OutcomeFork from "./OutcomeFork.astro";
---

<DiagramShell
  title="Data-flow and trust boundaries"
  caption="Numbered directional data flows across customer-controlled, BeaconGuard runtime, evidence-provider, governed-system, and management trust boundaries. The Control Plane is outside the request path. The customer IdP does not decide ALLOW or DENY."
  className="bg-diagram--dfd"
>
  <div
    class="bg-dfd-flow"
    role="img"
    aria-label="Data-flow diagram with numbered directional flows and trust boundaries"
  >
    <section class="bg-dfd-zone" aria-label="Customer-controlled boundary">
      <h4 class="bg-dfd-zone-title">Customer-controlled boundary</h4>
      <div class="bg-flow-step" data-dfd-node="app">Enterprise Application</div>
      <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
      <p class="bg-dfd-flow-label">1. Request context</p>
      <div class="bg-flow-step bg-flow-step--optional" data-dfd-node="connector">
        Optional System Connector
        <span class="bg-flow-step-detail">Non-evaluating</span>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
      <div class="bg-flow-step" data-dfd-node="idp">Customer Identity Provider</div>
      <p class="bg-dfd-flow-label">
        2. Trusted identity context → runtime verification
        <span class="bg-dfd-flow-sub">
          (customer-controlled; IdP does not decide ALLOW or DENY)
        </span>
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
    <p class="bg-dfd-flow-label">
      3. Normalized request context + identity context → runtime
    </p>

    <section
      class="bg-dfd-zone bg-dfd-zone--runtime"
      aria-label="BeaconGuard runtime boundary"
    >
      <h4 class="bg-dfd-zone-title">BeaconGuard runtime boundary</h4>

      <div class="bg-flow-step bg-flow-step--boundary" data-dfd-node="runtime">
        Runtime Control Boundary
        <span class="bg-flow-step-detail">Deterministic evaluation</span>
      </div>

      <div
        class="bg-dfd-store-row"
        aria-label="Runtime stores feeding evaluation"
      >
        <div class="bg-dfd-store-link">
          <div class="bg-flow-arrow bg-flow-arrow--up" aria-hidden="true">↑</div>
          <p class="bg-dfd-flow-label">4. Active release → evaluation</p>
          <div class="bg-flow-step" data-dfd-node="release">
            Active Verified Release
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-dfd-store-link">
          <div class="bg-flow-arrow bg-flow-arrow--bidir" aria-hidden="true">
            ↕
          </div>
          <p class="bg-dfd-flow-label">5. Replay verify ↔ shared state</p>
          <div class="bg-flow-step" data-dfd-node="replay">
            Shared Replay State
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
      <div class="bg-flow-step bg-flow-step--decision" data-dfd-node="decision">
        Determine ALLOW or DENY
      </div>
      <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
      <div class="bg-flow-step bg-outcome-evidence" data-dfd-node="vdr">
        <strong>Generate / Persist Verifiable Decision Record</strong>
        <span>Runtime action — record is written outward</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
    <p class="bg-dfd-flow-label">
      6. Write decision record → evidence-provider boundary
    </p>

    <section
      class="bg-dfd-zone bg-dfd-zone--evidence"
      aria-label="Evidence-provider boundary"
    >
      <h4 class="bg-dfd-zone-title">Evidence-provider boundary</h4>
      <div class="bg-flow-step" data-dfd-node="evidence-provider">
        Configured Evidence Provider
        <span class="bg-flow-step-detail">
          Separate supporting trust boundary — not part of the Runtime Control
          Boundary
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
      <div class="bg-flow-step bg-outcome-evidence" data-dfd-node="stored-vdr">
        Stored Verifiable Decision Records
      </div>
      <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
      <p class="bg-dfd-flow-label">
        7. Write success / verification result → runtime outcome path
      </p>
      <p class="bg-flow-note">
        Retention, integrity, and durability depend on the configured evidence
        provider — not universally append-only.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
    <p class="bg-dfd-flow-label">
      Outcomes after successful evidence persistence (mutually exclusive)
    </p>

    <OutcomeFork
      allowLabel="8. Forward to Governed AI / API / Automated System"
      denyLabel="9. Return DENY to Enterprise Application — no downstream execution"
      forkLabel="Outcomes after evidence persistence (mutually exclusive)"
    />

    <section
      class="bg-dfd-zone bg-dfd-zone--governed"
      aria-label="Governed downstream boundary"
    >
      <h4 class="bg-dfd-zone-title">Governed downstream-system boundary</h4>
      <div class="bg-flow-step bg-outcome-allow" data-dfd-node="governed">
        Governed AI / API / Automated System
        <span class="bg-flow-step-detail">
          Reached only on ALLOW after successful evidence persistence
        </span>
      </div>
      <p class="bg-flow-note">
        DENY path (flow 9) returns to the Enterprise Application with no
        governed-system execution.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      class="bg-dfd-zone bg-dfd-zone--mgmt"
      aria-label="Management-plane boundary"
    >
      <h4 class="bg-dfd-zone-title">
        Management-plane boundary (outside request path)
      </h4>
      <div class="bg-flow" role="list">
        <div class="bg-flow-step" role="listitem" data-dfd-node="operator">
          Operator / Administrator
        </div>
        <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        <p class="bg-dfd-flow-label">10. Administration</p>
        <div class="bg-flow-step" role="listitem" data-dfd-node="control-plane">
          Control Plane
          <span class="bg-flow-step-detail">Playbook and release lifecycle</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        <p class="bg-dfd-flow-label">
          11–12. Controlled distribution → verification → activation
        </p>
        <div
          class="bg-flow-step bg-outcome-evidence"
          role="listitem"
          data-dfd-node="mgmt-release"
        >
          Active Verified Release (feeds runtime evaluation — flow 4)
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="bg-flow-note">
      13. Monitoring or review may read evidence where configured. Evidence
      retention and integrity remain provider-dependent.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div slot="text">
    <ol>
      <li>
        Customer-controlled: Enterprise Application → Optional System Connector
        (request context).
      </li>
      <li>
        Customer Identity Provider supplies trusted identity context for runtime
        verification; does not decide ALLOW or DENY.
      </li>
      <li>
        Normalized request and identity context enter the BeaconGuard Runtime
        Boundary.
      </li>
      <li>Active Verified Release feeds deterministic evaluation.</li>
      <li>Replay verification uses Shared Replay State.</li>
      <li>
        Runtime generates and writes the Verifiable Decision Record to the
        separate Evidence-provider boundary.
      </li>
      <li>
        Write success / verification result returns to the outcome path;
        outcomes depend on successful evidence persistence.
      </li>
      <li>
        ALLOW forwards to the governed system only after successful evidence
        persistence.
      </li>
      <li>
        DENY returns to the Enterprise Application with no downstream execution.
      </li>
      <li>Operator / Administrator → Control Plane (outside request path).</li>
      <li>
        Control Plane manages Compliance Playbook release lifecycle through
        distribution, verification, and activation.
      </li>
      <li>
        Active Verified Release feeds runtime evaluation (flow 4).
      </li>
      <li>
        Monitoring or review may access evidence where configured;
        provider-dependent retention and integrity.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</DiagramShell>
